***************************
* SET UP THE INITIAL DATA *
***************************

NAME          SROSENBRNE

*   Problem :
*   *********

*   The separable extension of Rosenbrock's function.
*   This is a nonlinear equation variant of SROSENBR

*   Source:  problem 21 in
*   J.J. More', B.S. Garbow and K.E. Hillstrom,
*   "Testing Unconstrained Optimization Software",
*   ACM Transactions on Mathematical Software, vol. 7(1), pp. 17-41, 1981.

*   SIF input: Ph. Toint, Dec 1989.
*              Nick Gould (nonlinear equation version), Jan 2019
*              added 2nd (correct) starting point as SROSENBR, Pim Heeman, Jun 2026

*   classification NOR2-AN-V-V

*   N/2 is half the number of variables

*IE N/2                 5              $-PARAMETER n = 10     original value
*IE N/2                 25             $-PARAMETER n = 50
*IE N/2                 50             $-PARAMETER n = 100
*IE N/2                 250            $-PARAMETER n = 500
*IE N/2                 500            $-PARAMETER n = 1000
 IE N/2                 2500           $-PARAMETER n = 5000
*IE N/2                 5000           $-PARAMETER n = 10000

*   Number of variables

 IM N         N/2       2

*   Penalty parameter

 RE ALPHA               100.0
 RD SCALE     ALPHA     1.0
 R( RSCALE    SQRT                     SCALE

*   Other parameters

 IE 1                   1

VARIABLES

 DO I         1                        N
 X  X(I)
 ND

GROUPS

 DO I         1                        N/2
 IM 2I        I         2
 IA 2I-1      2I        -1
 XE GA(I)     X(2I)     1.0
 ZE GA(I)     'SCALE'                  RSCALE
 XE GB(I)     X(2I-1)   1.0
 ND

CONSTANTS

 DO I         1                        N/2
 X  SROSENBR  GB(I)     1.0
 ND

BOUNDS

 FR SROSENBR  'DEFAULT'

START POINT

 DO I         1                        N/2
 IM 2I        I         2
 IA 2I-1      2I        -1
 X  SROSENBR  X(2I)     1.0
 X  SROSENBR  X(2I-1)   1.2
* A minus sign to SROSENBR was originally in the wrong field
* such that it would get cut off, and hence SROSENBR2.
 X  SROSENBR2 X(2I)     1.0
 X  SROSENBR2 X(2I-1)   -1.2
 ND

ELEMENT TYPE

 EV MSQ       X

ELEMENT USES

 DO I         1                        N/2
 IM 2I        I         2
 IA 2I-1      2I        -1
 XT E(I)      MSQ
 ZV E(I)      X                        X(2I-1)
 ND

GROUP USES

 DO I         1                        N/2
 XE GA(I)     E(I)
 ND

OBJECT BOUND

*   Least square problems are bounded below by zero

 LO SROSENBR            0.0

*   Solution

*LO SOLTN               0.0

ENDATA

***********************
* SET UP THE FUNCTION *
* AND RANGE ROUTINES  *
***********************

ELEMENTS      SROSENBRNE

INDIVIDUALS

 T  MSQ
 F                      - X * X
 G  X                   - ( X + X )
 H  X         X         -2.0

ENDATA
